the page is genuinely reachable + deep-linkable without displacing any sibling; AppRouteParser gains the
"/charging/schedule" -> .smartCharge alias. Only the two exhaustive AppRoute switches (systemImage, group) +
pathSegment were touched. RouteTests invariants still hold (unique pathSegments — "smart-charge" is unique;
every route resolves to its group). No sibling registration or WatchDeepLink (its own enum) was altered. The
model is built @MainActor in the registration enum and captured, mirroring the sibling *RouteRegistration enums.

Data-state mapping (manifest "implement loading/empty/error/success for EVERY data source"):
  useRatePlans   : loading -> settings panel under .smartChargeRedacted(.placeholder); empty/error -> the three
                   hardcoded fallback options (web ratePlanOptions.length>0 ? mapped : fallbacks); success -> mapped name (utility) options.
  useChargePlans : loading -> SmartChargeSkeleton redaction; empty -> TSEmptyState("chargePlanner.noHistory")
                   (bound to model.historyIsEmpty); error -> SmartChargePageModel.phase .error -> errorView TSErrorDisplay+Retry; success -> SmartChargeHistoryTable.
  useOptimizeCharge: loading -> optimize TSButton isLoading spinner; error -> inline optimizeError text
                   (chargePlanner.optimizeError); success -> result panels (rate timeline + cost cards + schedule).
  useApplySchedule : loading -> apply TSButton isLoading spinner; error -> inline applyError text
                   (chargePlanner.applyError); success -> "Schedule Applied!" confirmation chip (chargePlanner.applied).

